# The provenance block on every stage row records the git blob hash of the prompt
# files and reference images that produced it, and a test asserts those hashes
# equal `git hash-object`. That equality only holds if what git stored matches the
# bytes on disk, so line-ending handling is pinned here rather than left to a
# contributor's core.autocrlf.

# Prompts are text and are hashed as LF.
prompts/**      text eol=lf

# Reference images are JPEGs. EOL normalization would corrupt them, and a
# corrupted reference degrades street detection corpus-wide with no error
# anywhere — the same failure mode reference_images.py guards against.
references/**   -text
